    "hardest_part": "Maintaining fast, accurate document inspection as requirements accumulate, using only one screenshot-grounded click or drag per turn. Reaching day 29 and a qualifying ending within three hours requires both efficient routine processing and careful handling of consequential story events.",
    "likely_failure": "Running out of wall-clock time before the late-day milestones. Other likely failures are accumulating inspection penalties and insufficient wages, or making a late story decision that produces a nonqualifying ending.",
    "helpful_mechanics": "The simulation pauses while I think, allowing careful inspection without directly consuming the workday clock. Rules and reference materials are available in the interface, document layouts become familiar, and repeatable inspection routines can reduce errors. Early citation tolerance provides some margin, and the scoring rewards intermediate progress rather than requiring a successful ending for all credit.",
    "harmful_mechanics": "Each document movement, reference lookup, stamp action, and handoff requires a separate input and screenshot cycle. Small text and crowded documents can cause visual mistakes. The running workday clock limits earnings during execution, while rent, food, heat, illness, and penalties constrain survival. Later requirements and story branches increase both action costs and the risk of an irreversible mistake."
